 "result_text": "I fixed the bad fractional part in `pysubs2/substation.py`. A time that rounds up to the next second now carries into the seconds instead of printing `.100`.\n\nI checked it with two inputs that round up across a second boundary. Both print `1:17:40.00`. I didn't run the CLI on the example file or the test suite.\n\n`ms_to_timestamp` split the time into hours, minutes, seconds and milliseconds first. It then rounded the milliseconds to centiseconds, so 995\u2013999 ms became 100 centiseconds. It now rounds the whole time to the nearest 10 ms first and splits it afterwards. The rounding still follows Aegisub's.",
